On Sun, Dec 14, 2014 at 3:56 PM, Alex Burka <aburka@seas.upenn.edu> wrote:
>
>  By the way, if I modify the "onset" rule from
>
> onset <- h / consonant? glide / initial
>
> to
>
> onset <- h / glide / initial
>
> This cuts out {saskrkuarka}, but {bangrblgaria} is saved by being parsed
> as {ban,gr,bl,GAR,ia} (whereas with the current PEG it parses as
> {ban,gr,bl,GA,ria}).
>
> Is this how we would do it, if we end up prohibiting some or all CgV, or
> would it be more restrictive, like adding "!glide" at the end of the
> "consonant" rule (which does kill both of these examples)?
>

I'd say !glide after each consonant, same as !h. If we add it in the
consonant rule, it would still allow a glide after a consonantal syllable,
I think. This however would mean that CG is disallowed in all cmevla, and
some traditional cmevla like "nitcion" become illegal.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

